      <h2>1. Who we are and how to contact us</h2>
      <p>“Paver Blocks”, “we”, “us” and “our” refer to the Paver Blocks business represented publicly by Mithal Shahan, Civil Contractor, based in Hyderabad, Sindh, Pakistan.</p>
      <p><strong>Website:</strong> <a href="https://paverblocks.com.pk/">paverblocks.com.pk</a><br />
      <strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:hellopaverblocks@gmail.com">hellopaverblocks@gmail.com</a><br />
      <strong>Phone and WhatsApp:</strong> <a href="tel:+923162753210">+92 316 2753210</a><br />
      <strong>Location:</strong> Hyderabad, Sindh, Pakistan</p>
      <p>If a different registered legal entity is responsible for a particular transaction, its legal name and relevant details should be identified in that transaction’s quotation, invoice or contract.</p>

      <h2>2. Acceptance and scope of these terms</h2>
      <p>These terms apply to your access to and use of this website, your submission of enquiries or quotation requests, and discussions or transactions with us, except to the extent that a separate written agreement applies.</p>
      <p>By using the website, you agree to follow the website-use provisions below. Submitting an enquiry does not by itself mean that we have accepted an order or entered into a project contract. A project or sale becomes binding only when the relevant terms have been confirmed through an accepted written quotation, order confirmation, contract or other clear written agreement.</p>
      <p>If a signed contract, accepted quotation, invoice or project-specific document conflicts with these general terms, the project-specific document will govern that transaction to the extent of the conflict. Mandatory rights under applicable law remain unaffected.</p>

      <h2>3. Website information and permitted use</h2>
      <p>You may use this website to learn about our services, view the information we publish and contact us about a potential project. You must use it lawfully and must not:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Submit information that you know to be false, misleading, unlawful or unauthorized.</li>
        <li>Attempt to disrupt, damage, probe or gain unauthorized access to the website, its hosting, forms, systems or administrative areas.</li>
        <li>Upload malware, spam, malicious code or material that infringes another person’s rights.</li>
        <li>Use automated methods to overload, scrape or misuse the website, except where permitted by law or with our written permission.</li>
        <li>Copy, republish or commercially exploit website content in a way that violates these terms or another party’s rights.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We may restrict access or take reasonable steps to protect the website where we detect misuse, security risks or unlawful activity.</p>

      <h2>4. Our services and product sourcing</h2>
      <p>Our listed work includes paver block installation, road construction and paving, footpath construction, parking area construction, industrial flooring-related civil work, and enquiries for government or private contracts. The services actually available for a particular location and project depend on the agreed scope, site conditions, resources and written project arrangements.</p>
      <p>Paver Blocks focuses on installation and paving-related civil work and does not represent itself as the manufacturer of paver blocks. Where product sourcing is discussed, products may be supplied by independent manufacturers or suppliers. Any supplier, manufacturer, product availability, specification, price or lead-time information is subject to confirmation by the relevant provider and the written terms of the transaction.</p>
      <p>We do not claim to control an independent manufacturer’s production process or the terms of a third-party supplier. Where we arrange or coordinate sourcing, the responsibility and contractual role of each party should be clear in the relevant quotation or order document.</p>

      <h2>5. Enquiries and quotations</h2>
      <p>You may contact us through the website, telephone, email or WhatsApp to discuss a project or request a quotation. Please provide accurate information about the site, location, measurements, intended use, specifications and other relevant requirements.</p>
      <p>An enquiry is a request for discussion or pricing, not an accepted order. Any quotation we issue is subject to the assumptions, scope, exclusions, price, validity period (if stated), availability and other conditions written in that quotation. A quotation may need to be revised if the information supplied is incomplete or changes, site conditions differ from those described, specifications are altered, or supplier costs or availability change before acceptance.</p>
      <p>Do not rely on an estimate, website description or informal discussion as a final project price or scope where a formal written quotation or contract is required. The quotation or project document should identify the agreed work and any material exclusions.</p>

      <h2>6. Product descriptions, colours and specifications</h2>
      <p>We aim to describe services and display product or project information accurately. Website photographs, illustrations, colours, patterns and examples are for general information and may not exactly represent the finished result or the appearance of materials at a particular site.</p>
      <p>Actual paver appearance can vary with manufacturer, production batch, raw materials, lighting, display settings, weathering and installation conditions. Dimensions, technical performance, load suitability, colour, pattern and other specifications should be confirmed against the relevant manufacturer documentation, sample or written project specification before an order is accepted.</p>
      <p>Where a particular material, brand, grade, sample or technical standard is essential, it must be clearly identified in the accepted quotation or contract. We will not treat a general website image as a guaranteed product specification.</p>

      <h2>7. Orders and contract formation</h2>
      <p>Orders may be discussed through a quotation process or another ordering method that we expressly make available. We are not obliged to accept an enquiry or proposed order. Before work or supply begins, the parties should confirm in writing the relevant scope, quantities, specifications, price, payment arrangements, delivery or installation responsibilities, schedule assumptions and any special conditions.</p>
      <p>An online form or message sent through this website is an enquiry unless the website expressly provides an order-acceptance process and we confirm acceptance through that process. A payment request, receipt or order confirmation should be read together with the applicable quotation or contract.</p>

      <h2>8. Prices, taxes and payment arrangements</h2>
      <p>Prices and payment obligations are those stated in the quotation, accepted order, invoice or contract for the relevant transaction. Unless expressly stated in that document, website content does not establish a price, deposit, advance-payment percentage, instalment schedule, credit facility, accepted payment method or payment due date.</p>
      <p>Any applicable taxes, duties, transport charges, site costs or other amounts should be identified in the relevant quotation or invoice. Please confirm the payment recipient and payment instructions using an official written document or a contact channel you have independently verified. Do not send card security codes, passwords or banking credentials through our general enquiry form or chat.</p>
      <p>Where an electronic payment option is expressly offered, its displayed terms and the relevant payment provider’s conditions will also apply. We do not currently promise that online checkout or any particular payment gateway is available for every order.</p>

      <h2>9. Changes to project scope</h2>
      <p>Any change to quantities, materials, design, dimensions, site conditions, work sequence or other agreed requirements may affect the price, resources and completion schedule. Changes should be agreed in writing before the changed work is carried out, including any adjustment to cost or timing.</p>
      <p>We may need to pause affected work while a material change, safety concern, access issue or additional requirement is clarified. Work outside the agreed scope is not included unless it is accepted in writing.</p>

      <h2>10. Site access and customer responsibilities</h2>
      <p>Where a project requires access to a site, the customer or site representative must provide the access, permissions, information and coordination that the quotation or contract assigns to them. This may include identifying site boundaries and underground or concealed services, arranging relevant permissions, providing a safe working area, coordinating with other contractors and notifying us of known site hazards or restrictions.</p>
      <p>Responsibility for surveys, design, excavation, sub-base preparation, drainage, disposal, traffic management, utility relocation, permits and other preparatory or associated work must be established in the project documents. These items are not automatically included merely because paving or installation has been requested.</p>
      <p>If the site is materially different from the information provided, inaccessible or unsafe, the parties should agree how to address the issue before affected work proceeds.</p>

      <h2>11. Delivery, collection and installation</h2>
      <p>Whether materials are delivered, collected or installed, and who arranges transport, unloading, storage, equipment and site handling, must be stated in the accepted quotation or contract. Delivery locations, charges, dates, time windows and any minimum access requirements are not guaranteed by general website content.</p>
      <p>Any estimated schedule is subject to the written assumptions and may be affected by weather, site readiness, access, supplier availability, transport, approvals, changes in scope and events outside reasonable control. We will communicate material changes through an agreed contact channel where reasonably practicable.</p>
      <p>Installation methods and the expected finished result depend on the agreed specification and actual site conditions. No installation work is included in a product-only supply unless the relevant document expressly says so.</p>

      <h2>12. Inspection, completion and reporting concerns</h2>
      <p>The customer should arrange a reasonable inspection of supplied materials or completed work and notify us promptly in writing of any apparent shortage, damage, mismatch or workmanship concern, with relevant photographs and order details where possible.</p>
      <p>Any inspection, handover, acceptance process, defect-notification period or remedy applicable to a project should be set out in its contract or quotation. A request to inspect or report a concern does not remove rights or remedies that cannot lawfully be excluded or restricted.</p>

      <h2>13. Cancellations, returns and refunds</h2>
      <p>Cancellation, return, exchange, refund and any applicable charges or deductions depend on the accepted quotation, order, contract, the status of work or supply, the nature of the goods or services and applicable law. The relevant written transaction document should state any agreed cancellation process and financial consequences.</p>
      <p>We do not publish a universal cancellation deadline, automatic refund entitlement, non-refundable advance rule or blanket exclusion for custom or specially sourced materials in these general terms. Please obtain written confirmation of the applicable arrangements before accepting an order or making a payment. Nothing in this section limits a consumer right or remedy that applicable law does not allow the parties to exclude.</p>
      <p>To raise a cancellation, return or refund request, contact us using the details in Section 22 and include your quotation, order or invoice reference.</p>

      <h2>14. Warranty and defects</h2>
      <p>Any express warranty, workmanship commitment, product guarantee, maintenance obligation or defect remedy must be stated in the applicable quotation, contract, manufacturer warranty or other written transaction document. Its duration, coverage, exclusions and claim process are determined by that document and applicable law.</p>
      <p>We do not create a general warranty period or promise a particular product lifespan through this website. Where products are made or warranted by an independent manufacturer, the manufacturer’s applicable warranty terms may govern product-related claims. This does not remove any responsibility that we have expressly accepted in writing or that cannot lawfully be excluded.</p>

      <h2>15. Intellectual property and website materials</h2>
      <p>Unless otherwise stated, the website design, text, branding, graphics, photographs and other content are owned by us or used with permission. You may view and use them for personal, non-commercial reference when considering our services. You must not reproduce, modify, distribute or commercially use our content without permission, except where applicable law allows it.</p>
      <p>Third-party names, logos, product images and trademarks remain the property of their respective owners. Their appearance on this website does not necessarily imply endorsement, agency or partnership.</p>

      <h2>16. Third-party websites and providers</h2>
      <p>This website may link to external websites or services, including messaging, hosting, security, manufacturers, suppliers or payment providers. Those services are operated by third parties and may have separate terms, privacy notices, availability and fees. We are not responsible for content or services outside our reasonable control. A link is provided for convenience and does not by itself constitute an endorsement.</p>

      <h2>17. Liability and legal rights</h2>
      <p>We take reasonable care in preparing website information, but the website is provided for general information and may not always be complete, current or suitable for a particular project. You should obtain project-specific measurements, technical advice and written specifications before making a construction or purchasing decision.</p>
      <p>To the extent permitted by applicable law, we are not responsible for indirect or consequential loss arising solely from use of general website information, or for loss caused by inaccurate information supplied by a customer, third-party supplier conduct outside our responsibility, unauthorized use of the website or events beyond our reasonable control.</p>
      <p>Nothing in these terms excludes or limits liability, a consumer guarantee, statutory right or remedy where that exclusion or limitation is prohibited by applicable law. Any liability relating to a specific project will be determined by its contract and applicable law.</p>

      <h2>18. Events outside reasonable control</h2>
      <p>Neither party will be treated as in breach to the extent performance is delayed or prevented by events beyond its reasonable control, such as severe weather, flooding, fire, natural disaster, epidemic, public emergency, war, civil disturbance, government action, transport disruption, widespread utility or communications failure, or a material supplier disruption that could not reasonably be avoided.</p>
      <p>The affected party should notify the other as soon as reasonably practicable. The parties should discuss reasonable steps to reduce the impact and agree any revised schedule or other appropriate arrangement. This section does not remove payment obligations for work or goods already properly supplied, or rights that cannot lawfully be excluded.</p>

      <h2>19. Privacy and communications</h2>
      <p>Our handling of personal information is explained in our <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>. By contacting us, you acknowledge that we may use the information you provide to respond to your enquiry, prepare a quotation, communicate about a project or administer a transaction, in accordance with that policy and applicable law.</p>
      <p>We may communicate with you using the contact details and channels you provide, including telephone, email or WhatsApp. Please keep your contact details accurate and tell us if your preferred contact method changes.</p>

      <h2>20. International visitors and applicable law</h2>
      <p>Our business is based in Hyderabad, Sindh, Pakistan. We welcome enquiries from Pakistan and other locations, but the availability of services, ability to supply or install, applicable taxes, import or export requirements, local permissions and consumer protections may differ by country and project.</p>
      <p>Unless a project-specific contract states otherwise to the extent legally permitted, these general terms and any non-contractual matters arising from them are governed by the laws of Pakistan. Disputes are subject to the competent courts in Pakistan, without limiting any mandatory consumer protection, jurisdictional or other rights that apply to you under the law of your location.</p>

      <h2>21. Updates, severability and entire agreement</h2>
      <p>We may update these terms when our website, services, business arrangements or legal requirements change. The “Last updated” date at the top of this page identifies the current version. Changes apply from publication to future website use and, where relevant, future transactions; they do not retrospectively alter an already signed agreement unless the parties agree or applicable law permits.</p>
      <p>If a provision is found unenforceable, the remaining provisions continue to apply to the extent permitted by law. A failure or delay in enforcing a provision does not waive the right to enforce it later. These general terms, together with any applicable accepted quotation, order or contract, describe the relevant agreement between the parties.</p>

      <h2>22. Contact and questions</h2>
      <p>For questions about these terms, a quotation, order or project, contact:</p>
      <p><strong>Paver Blocks — Terms &amp; Conditions Enquiries</strong><br />
      By Mithal Shahan, Civil Contractor<br />
      Hyderabad, Sindh, Pakistan<br />
      Email: <a href="mailto:hellopaverblocks@gmail.com">hellopaverblocks@gmail.com</a><br />
      Phone / WhatsApp: <a href="tel:+923162753210">+92 316 2753210</a></p>
      <p>Please include your quotation, order or invoice reference where applicable. Do not include passwords or payment-card security details in your message.</p>
